{
  "id": "diencephalic-amnesia",
  "term": "diencephalic amnesia",
  "definition": "Diencephalic amnesia is amnesia associated with damage to an extended network of subcortical structures connected with the hippocampal formation, especially within the diencephalon. It refers to memory impairment arising from this broader brain network rather than from the hippocampus alone.",
